# Root .gitignore (rename to .gitignore) — WHOLE-REPO concerns ONLY.
#
# The rule: this file lists only what belongs to no single sub-project — OS noise, editor state,
# agent scratch. Everything a sub-project owns lives in THAT sub-project's file:
# backend/.gitignore (.venv, __pycache__, .env, data/) and frontend/.gitignore (node_modules,
# dist). Don't restate them here.
#
# Why: git reads the nearest .gitignore, so a `backend/.venv/` line up here buys nothing the
# sub-project file doesn't already cover — it just rots the day someone renames a folder, and it
# splits "what does the backend ignore?" across two files. Note too that a bare `.venv/` already
# matches at ANY depth, so a root `.venv/` plus a `backend/.venv/` was always one rule written
# twice.

# macOS / Windows
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Agent / assistant scratch
.claude/
